{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor opened with generic reassurance and medication continuation without first screening for acute stroke/bleeding red flags from a post-stroke patient on dual antithrombotics. Later turns eventually asked about symptoms and bleeding, but the initial turn treated a blurry family account as complete and gave BP target advice without linking to stroke risk. That constitutes a serious RC1 omission (unsafe triage before routine interpretation). Because one serious in-chain error is present, the trajectory grade is 1 regardless of any later strengths. High-order points cannot rescue a grade-1 trajectory.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00310",
        "explanation": "The final family message shows the trajectory did not return to the doctor for a closing confirmation of teach-back or receipt of the safety plan, but the doctor had previously been providing advice and the conversation was considered closed by the system.",
        "quote": "医生，我们现在看完神经内科出来了，还在门诊这边等取药/预约。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": false,
    "explanation": "The trajectory ends with the family still in the outpatient area and no explicit teach-back or closure from the doctor. Although the system marked it as closed_success, the doctor's final message is not a safe, traceable closure because the initial safety error was never repaired. The episode is bounded but the closure is not valid under the contract.",
    "label": "questionable_open",
    "safe": false,
    "traceable": false
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
        "explanation": "The first doctor message gives general advice about continuing medications and getting tests without screening for acute stroke symptoms or bleeding risks from dual antithrombotics.",
        "quote": "血压 156/95 仍偏高，属\"二级高血压\"水平，提示目前降压方案可能还不够，需要尽快把血压压到 130/80 以下。"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
        "explanation": "The doctor interprets BP as needing to be lowered to 130/80 without contextualizing the prior stroke and carotid occlusion risk, missing the case-specific urgency.",
        "quote": "需要尽快把血压压到 130/80 以下。"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00059",
        "explanation": "The doctor later references the family's initial medication list but still does not integrate the prior stroke and carotid occlusion into the urgency of the plan.",
        "quote": "利伐沙班＋氯吡格雷是“双抗栓”组合，用于脑梗合并房颤或严重动脉狭窄"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
        "explanation": "The doctor fails to ask about acute neurologic symptoms or bleeding in the initial message, missing the opportunity to triage for red flags.",
        "quote": "如果收缩压连续两次≥160 或出现头晕、说话含糊、一侧手脚乏力，立刻就近急诊"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00357",
        "explanation": "The doctor later provided specific instructions for meal-dependent medication when the family reported a hypoglycemic episode, but the initial gap in safety overshadowed this.",
        "quote": "如果中午几乎不吃主食（米饭≤半碗或面条≤小撮），就把这顿阿卡波糖直接跳过"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
